{
  "_comment": [
    "Worked sequences built from Tooling Intelligence's own September 2026 ask",
    "(Steuart Durham, routed via Jamie). These are the acceptance cases for the",
    "sequence builder: if the CMS can express these three, it can express what TI",
    "described. Seed them with: node test/seed-examples.js [baseUrl]",
    "",
    "ARCHITECTURE: step 1 is the 3D login clip. Everything after it is the Web",
    "Object. Log out hands control back to Storyline for the closing 3D. The",
    "physical acts are screen states, not renders, so nothing multiplies by",
    "product type or hardware type.",
    "",
    "TI_EXAMPLE_1 is a straightforward single take.",
    "TI_EXAMPLE_2 is the product-kit case, where the same door-open beat repeats",
    "four times in a row. Repeatability is the engineering work, because Storyline",
    "layers show once and have no loops or arrays.",
    "TI_EXAMPLE_3 exercises the events that were not in the original build:",
    "fingerprint login, the handheld scanner cradle and a Scale location.",
    "",
    "Product steps reference catalogue ids from shared/catalogue.js. Name, part",
    "number, quantity, unit of issue, device type, menu number and door code are",
    "all resolved from there, the way the real screens derive them."
  ],
